WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: we're continuing to track&nbsp;
what's happening with this Omicron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:10.560
variant and booster mandates are starting.&nbsp;
The United Kingdom is setting new records.&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.320
Speaker 2: It is an
Speaker 1: explosion of information and of panic.&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.469
Speaker 2: And I
Speaker 1: understand the&nbsp;

00:00:16.469 --> 00:00:20.160
Speaker 2: worry, and I
Speaker 1: also still don't know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.680
it is warranted on the basis of what we
Speaker 2: know about Omicron.&nbsp;

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.040
Speaker 1: So let's go
Speaker 2: through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.560
a few different
Speaker 1: aspects here.&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.160
Speaker 2: Businesses, many
Speaker 1: employers and universities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.480
are now saying fully vaccinated
Speaker 2: means three shots,&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.880
Speaker 1: not two.
Speaker 2: Now, however&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.960
Speaker 1: serious Omicron is the early
Speaker 2: data. The early data&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.920
Speaker 1: is that if you have three shots, you&nbsp;
are significantly less likely to get a symptomatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.320
infection of Omicron than if you have two shots&nbsp;
now on asymptomatic. We don't yet really know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.840
on effectiveness on against
Speaker 2: serious illness&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.360
Speaker 1: or death. We're still getting&nbsp;
information. It seems three shots are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.320
somewhat better, but three shots&nbsp;
seem significantly better than two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:11.760
against Omicron, against symptomatic illness. So&nbsp;
that's really important. So the Metropolitan Opera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.840
yesterday said if you want to be an
Speaker 2: eligible audience member&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.320
Speaker 1: or an employee,
Speaker 2: you need that third shot&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.600
Speaker 1: a Georgetown NYU. Some private&nbsp;
colleges have said you're going to need your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.360
third shot. Number of universities&nbsp;
where I know people working say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.600
when you come back for the spring semester,
Speaker 2: you've got to have that third&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.600
Speaker 1: shot. The NFL is requiring&nbsp;
coaches and staff to get booster shots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.120
by December 27th, and the
Speaker 2: real question here is what&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.080
Speaker 1: is actually going on with the&nbsp;
Omicron variant. And I know we continue to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:56.160
it's early. We still need more data. We still&nbsp;
need to wait. It continues to be that on average,&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.880
Speaker 2: if you get
Speaker 1: the Omicron variant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:04.160
you are less likely to get really, really sick
Speaker 2: by virtue of being more contagious,&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.840
Speaker 1: which it appears to&nbsp;
be. The burden on society can&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.800
Speaker 2: still be large,
Speaker 1: and we are seeing even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.480
advance of Omicron being the reason. Even still&nbsp;
with Delta, we're starting to see hospitals in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.040
different states increasingly
Speaker 2: fill up,&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.749
Speaker 1: so that's one aspect of&nbsp;
what's going on. The CDC has issued a&nbsp;

00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:27.280
Speaker 2: forecast that cases
Speaker 1: weekly are going to be up to&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.760
Speaker 2: 1.3
Speaker 1: million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:38.800
by Christmas Day and that deaths are going to&nbsp;
surge 73 percent to over 15000 a week when and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.600
as Omicron becomes the dominant strain. And&nbsp;
again, some people hear that and they say,&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.760
Speaker 2: well, hold on a second. If it's less
Speaker 1: serious, why would deaths go up? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.920
again, you could have something that's half&nbsp;
as serious but three times as contagious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.520
and you would still see deaths go&nbsp;
up 50 percent. I mean, it's very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.760
very crude math that doesn't exactly work
Speaker 2: that way, but that's basically the way&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.720
Speaker 1: that it is. In the meantime,&nbsp;
the UK is seeing absolutely record cases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.120
A number of different countries are seeing&nbsp;
really, really insane numbers. And the good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.760
news, if there is any in
Speaker 2: the UK is that&nbsp;

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.709
Speaker 1: while the cases are going up&nbsp;
dramatically as Omicron takes over, deaths due to&nbsp;

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:23.360
Speaker 2: COVID are actually
Speaker 1: down over the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.280
two weeks. Now that may
Speaker 2: reverse what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.080
what's the what's the possible
Speaker 1: counterpoint to?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.840
It's very spreadable, but less&nbsp;
severe. The counterpoint would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.760
what if there is more of a delay before you&nbsp;
get really sick? In other words, we I think&nbsp;

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.400
Speaker 2: at one point the average
Speaker 1: interval between infection and death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.520
was 17 days. At one point, it doesn't really&nbsp;
matter, but at one point it was roughly 17 days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.400
Is it possible that Omicron causes&nbsp;
mild disease for, I don't know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.200
five weeks. And then you get really
Speaker 2: sick and die?&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.360
Speaker 1: Doctors say it's possible, but&nbsp;
it's not very likely. So that's the good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:08.720
news so far that. We can point to lastly, the&nbsp;
White House, there's been this question of would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:14.640
the U.S. shut down again to the extent that the&nbsp;
U.S. ever did shut down? I think the answer is&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.560
Speaker 2: no for a couple of different
Speaker 1: reasons, unless there were to be a more&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.720
Speaker 2: severe variant, which we don't seem to
Speaker 1: have at this point in time. Number one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.840
at the state level, there are very few&nbsp;
states at this point that seem willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.040
to do anything even remotely approximating&nbsp;
a shutdown. That's number one. Number two,&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.589
Speaker 2: the White House is saying we are not
Speaker 1: going to do that. We are&nbsp;

00:04:37.589 --> 00:04:42.560
Speaker 2: not going to have sweeping
Speaker 1: shutdowns, but we are seeing signs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.120
that certainly raised questions as to what the&nbsp;
policy should be the hospitals becoming overrun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.800
Events being postponed. Some colleges and&nbsp;
universities already going back to remote. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.200
there are signs. But the White House&nbsp;
insists it's not going to happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.200
again if you get your third shot, and&nbsp;
that actually is 70 percent effective at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.400
preventing symptomatic illness.
Speaker 2: And this is a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.960
spreadable, but less serious variant.
Speaker 1: If people do the right things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:16.400
you shouldn't have to shut down. If the shutdowns&nbsp;
become a real possibility, it would overwhelmingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.160
be because a lot of people aren't doing&nbsp;
the things that are available to us to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.840
Let me know your thoughts. What do you think&nbsp;
will happen in the next one to two months?

